From: Armbian <info@armbian.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: k1x-emac: Add proper jumbo frame support

The k1x-emac driver allows changing MTU up to 4K via emac_change_mtu()
and allocates appropriately sized DMA buffers, but it never programs
the MAC_MAXIMUM_FRAME_SIZE and MAC_RECEIVE_JABBER_SIZE registers.

This causes the MAC hardware to reject frames larger than the default
1518 bytes, even when larger buffers are allocated. Frames exceeding
the default size trigger EMAC_RX_FRAME_JABBER_ERR and are discarded.

Fix this by:
1. Setting ndev->max_mtu in probe to allow MTU changes up to 4K
2. Programming MAC_MAXIMUM_FRAME_SIZE and MAC_RECEIVE_JABBER_SIZE
   in emac_init_hw() based on the configured buffer size

Signed-off-by: Armbian <info@armbian.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/spacemit/k1x-emac.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/spacemit/k1x-emac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/spacemit/k1x-emac.c
@@ -302,6 +302,12 @@ int emac_init_hw(struct emac_priv *priv)

 	emac_wr(priv, MAC_RECEIVE_PACKET_START_THRESHOLD, priv->rx_threshold);

+	/* Set maximum frame size based on configured buffer size to support
+	 * jumbo frames. Also set jabber size to prevent false jabber errors.
+	 */
+	emac_wr(priv, MAC_MAXIMUM_FRAME_SIZE, priv->dma_buf_sz);
+	emac_wr(priv, MAC_RECEIVE_JABBER_SIZE, priv->dma_buf_sz + 8);
+
 	/* set emac rx mitigation frame count */
 	val = EMAC_RX_FRAMES & MREGBIT_RECEIVE_IRQ_FRAME_COUNTER_MSK;

@@ -2660,6 +2666,9 @@ static int emac_probe(struct platform_de

 	ndev->hw_features = NETIF_F_SG;
 	ndev->features |= ndev->hw_features;
+
+	/* Allow MTU up to 4K buffer size minus ethernet overhead */
+	ndev->max_mtu = EMAC_RX_BUF_4K - ETH_HLEN - ETH_FCS_LEN;
 	priv = netdev_priv(ndev);
 	priv->ndev = ndev;
 	priv->pdev = pdev;
